  "id": "DrugBank_DB00588 - MONDO_15758",
  "verbalization": "Fluticasone Propionate appears to be linked to Primary Cutaneous T-cell Lymphoma through a chain of indications involving corticosteroids. The evidence suggests that Fluticasone Propionate may act as a precursor in the treatment of conditions like Granuloma Annulare and Contact Dermatitis, which in turn are associated with Desoximetasone and Prednicarbate, both of which are corticosteroids known to have immunosuppressive effects. These corticosteroids are implicated in the pathogenesis of Primary Cutaneous T-cell Lymphoma, potentially through mechanisms involving inflammation, immune modulation, or cellular proliferation. The shared use of corticosteroids in these conditions implies a possible underlying biological pathway where corticosteroid therapy may influence the development or progression of the lymphoma. The evidence is consistent with a hypothesis that Fluticasone Propionate, through its role in inducing or modulating inflammatory or immunological responses, could contribute to the development of Primary Cutaneous T-cell Lymphoma in certain patient populations.",
